Jon,
Common wisdom is that the best way to learn a language is to spend time where it's spoken, so the idea of a virtual-reality Lojbanistan has long appealed to me. The place that Lojban is spoken is really the MIRC channel, but there is no environment to point to or manipulate there. I had the idea to someday use one of those 3D avatar chat services if it were possible to patch the software to put a Lojban tag floating over every object in the environment.
